Z||000000||fierobob88||03-29-2001||11:03 AM||||Ok, I am looking to find an exhaust for my '88 4 cylindar.  I am wandering what is the best exhaust systems to go with and where I can order them from.  I would also like to know where I can find lowering springs other than the fiero store (I want more than an 1" drop).  Also, I was wandering why there are so many more suspension parts for the 84-87?||||reg||3
Z||000001||Mr.Frosty||03-29-2001||11:12 AM||||This brings up a good point.Did the 88' coupe<BR>have the same suspension as the earlier coupes,or was it the same as the Formula/GT<BR>for 88'?<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top <BR>85 GT Turbo||||reg||5
Z||000002||Rodrv6||03-29-2001||12:02 PM||||The reason there are so many more parts available for the 84-87's is that they made a lot more of them than the 88's.  Also, the 88's had a much improved suspension from the factory, so there is not as much need to upgrade them.<BR>All 88's had the same basic suspension whether a coupe or a GT. <P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
